From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] imageres: the system's images; shell32: icon 16739

Windows keeps many shared icons in imageres.dll -- the elevation shield,
documents, folders, the libraries -- and programs load them by resource id
(SHDefExtractIcon, ExtractIconEx, "imageres.dll,-1002"). Wine has no
imageres.dll, so each such icon failed to load; WireGuard for Windows' window
takes the icon it asked for as given and ended with a nil pointer panic in its
toolbar (i1012), and our own Libraries (6081) asked for icons that were not
there.

dlls/imageres is a data-only DLL with Wine's and Stained Glass OS's own images
(the art is not Microsoft's) under the ids programs ask for: 1, 2 (document),
3 and 4 (folder), 78 and 1028 (shield), 106 (secure), 174 (compressed folder),
1002-1005 (Documents, Pictures, Music and Videos libraries). shell32 gets icon
16739 (a change under way), which WireGuard shows while a tunnel starts.

Test: test/imageres-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit): each icon loads at 16 pixels
through SHDefExtractIcon of system32\<dll>.dll; fails on 1192 (no imageres).
---
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1190,6 +1190,7 @@
 enable_iertutil
 enable_imaadp32_acm
 enable_imagehlp
+enable_imageres
 enable_imm32
 enable_inetcomm
 enable_inetcpl_cpl
@@ -22441,6 +22442,7 @@
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imaadp32.acm enable_imaadp32_acm
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imagehlp enable_imagehlp
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imagehlp/tests enable_tests
+wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imageres enable_imageres
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imm.dll16 enable_win16
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imm32 enable_imm32
 wine_fn_config_makefile dlls/imm32/tests enable_tests
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2725,6 +2725,7 @@
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imaadp32.acm)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imagehlp)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imagehlp/tests)
+WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imageres)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imm.dll16,enable_win16)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imm32)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/imm32/tests)
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/imageres/Makefile.in
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+MODULE = imageres.dll
+
+EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--data-only
+
+SOURCES = \
+	imageres.rc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/imageres/imageres.rc
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+/*
+ * imageres.dll: the system's images (Stained Glass OS, i1012)
+ *
+ * Windows keeps many of its shared icons in imageres.dll, and programs load
+ * them by resource id (SHDefExtractIcon, ExtractIconEx, LoadImage with
+ * "imageres.dll,-N"): the elevation shield, documents and folders, the
+ * libraries. Wine had no imageres.dll, so every such icon failed to load --
+ * WireGuard for Windows' window took the missing icon for one and ended with
+ * a nil pointer panic. These are Wine's and Stained Glass OS's own images,
+ * under the ids programs ask for; the art is not Microsoft's.
